.TH CLOG_SET_LEVEL 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
clog_set_level \- change the minimum log level at runtime
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <clogger.h>

void clog_set_level(clog logger, clog_level_t level);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Updates the minimum severity level. Messages with a level strictly
below the new minimum are silently discarded on subsequent calls.
The change takes effect immediately and is visible to all threads
sharing the logger.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
logger  Logger handle.
level   New minimum level (CLOG_TRACE through CLOG_OFF).
        Use CLOG_OFF to suppress all output.
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
Thread-safe: the minimum level is a per-logger, atomically updated
value, independent of the lock that serialises writes/rotation for
the shared output target, so changing one logger's level never
contends with a write in progress on a sibling logger sharing the
same target.
Asserts if logger is CLOG_INVALID, stale, or already closed.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR clog_get_level (3),
.BR clog_open_fd_mp (3),
.BR clog_open_file_mp (3)
